WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
MCPSentry: the tools your agents trust, verified continuously — not once, at install time.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The problem: 29 percent of the most popular MCP servers carry a risk finding; more than a third of agent skills analysed were flawed; and 74 percent of organisations say their agents are over-permissioned.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:29.000
What it does: pins and hashes every approved tool at approval; alerts on drift and rug-pulls with the diff; covers private and local servers; scans skills and context files; audits permissions and identity; and exports an Agent Bill of Materials.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The deliverable: a monthly attestation statement — what was pinned, what drifted, how fast the alert came, the permission findings, the BOM. The figures shown are a sample.

5
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:50.000
How it ships: the free, open-source scanner in the first quarter of 2027; then inventory and pinning in week one, the watch in week two, and a statement every month.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Published licence prices: the scanner is free and open source; Attestation Team from $1,500 a month for up to 25 servers, $900 a month for early-access estates; Attestation Enterprise from $4,000 a month.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Early access in the first quarter of 2027 — rainkernel.com or hello@rainkernel.com.
